-- title:
--   Pull-back of the ideal sheaf of a global ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ and $Y$ be schemes (in a fixed universe), let $I$ be an ideal of the ring $\Gamma(Y,\top)$ of global sections of $\mathcal O_Y$, and let $f\colon X\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Mathlib's `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I` is the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf datum on $Y$ whose ideal on an affine open $V\subseteq Y$ is the image of $I$ under the restriction map $\Gamma(Y,\top)\to\Gamma(V,\mathcal O_Y)$, and `comap f` transports an ideal sheaf datum on $Y$ to one on $X$ (affine-locally, extension of ideals along the ring maps induced by $f$). The assertion is the equality of ideal sheaf data on $X$
--   $$(\text{ofIdealTop } I).\mathrm{comap}\, f = \text{ofIdealTop}\,\bigl(I\cdot\Gamma(X,\top)\bigr),$$
--   where the ideal on the right is the image `I.map f.appTop.hom` of $I$ under the ring homomorphism $f^{\sharp}\colon\Gamma(Y,\top)\to\Gamma(X,\top)$ induced by $f$ on global sections. Thus the inverse image along $f$ of the ideal sheaf generated by a global ideal is the ideal sheaf generated by the image of that ideal under $f^\sharp$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the formation of the closed subscheme cut out by an ideal of global functions with base change along an arbitrary morphism; specialised to a principal ideal $(r)$ it says that the pull-back of $V(r)\subseteq Y$ is $V(f^\sharp r)\subseteq X$. It is used in the project wherever ideal sheaves given by global equations have to be pulled back, for instance in the treatment of invertible ideal sheaves generated by one global section and in computations on projective space.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_comap_ofIdealTop.lean

import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Functorial

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

theorem AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_ofIdealTop
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Ideal Γ(Y, ⊤)) (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).comap f
      = Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (I.map f.appTop.hom) := by sorry
